1
00:02:05,310 --> 00:02:07,930
- Rider approaching! - Open the gate!

2
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:37,670
Why, it's the Prince of Winterfell.

3
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:41,540
- Envy isn't attractive. - What envy?

4
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,330
You should be proud of your brother's achievement.

5
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:47,320
I took the great castle of Winterfell with 20 men.

6
00:02:47,330 --> 00:02:48,990
You're a great warrior.

7
00:02:49,150 --> 00:02:51,320
I saw the bodies above your gates.

8
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:53,580
Which one gave you the tougher fight,

9
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:55,510
the cripple or the six-year-old?

10
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:59,960
I treated the Stark boys with honor

11
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,790
and they repaid me with treachery.

12
00:03:01,790 --> 00:03:05,000
You treated them with honor by butchering them?

13
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,590
Before I had to kill them, I treated them--

14
00:03:06,590 --> 00:03:09,130
You seized their home, as is your right.

15
00:03:09,130 --> 00:03:11,930
- We're Ironborn; We take what we need. - Exactly.

16
00:03:11,930 --> 00:03:14,740
Then you made them prisoners in their home and they ran away.

17
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:16,720
Is that treachery?

18
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:19,190
I'd call it bravery.

19
00:03:19,390 --> 00:03:20,820
They made me a promise--

20
00:03:20,820 --> 00:03:22,900
Your little boy prisoners made you a promise

21
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:24,970
and you got mad when they broke it?

22
00:03:25,490 --> 00:03:27,340
Are you the dumbest cunt alive?

23
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:29,270
- Don't call me a-- - A cunt.

24
00:03:29,270 --> 00:03:32,500
A dumb cunt who killed the only two Starks in Winterfell.

25
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:35,550
You know how valuable those boys were?

26
00:03:35,550 --> 00:03:38,270
If I hadn't killed them, the Northerners would think me weak.

27
00:03:38,270 --> 00:03:41,450
You are weak. And you're stupid.

28
00:03:41,450 --> 00:03:42,900
I'm warning you.

29
00:03:44,010 --> 00:03:45,390
Go on, then,

30
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:46,930
warn me.

31
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:53,100
You haven't brought enough men.

32
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:55,730
How am I supposed to defend Winterfell with just this lot?

33
00:03:55,730 --> 00:03:58,490
You're not. I've come to bring you home.

34
00:03:58,890 --> 00:04:01,160
- Father wants a word. - Is this a joke?

35
00:04:01,510 --> 00:04:03,070
Winterfell is the heart of the North.

36
00:04:03,070 --> 00:04:06,450
Aye, it is, hundreds of miles from the sea.

37
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:08,520
We're islanders, baby brother.

38
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:10,050
Had you forgotten that?

39
00:04:10,050 --> 00:04:12,490
Our power comes from our ships.

40
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:16,640
And now that you've decorated your walls with the bodies of the Stark boys,

41
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:19,990
every man in the North wants to see you hanged.

42
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:22,480
When Robb Stark finds out...

43
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:24,850
He won't find out. We've killed all the ravens.

44
00:04:24,850 --> 00:04:26,440
We have all the horses.

45
00:04:28,190 --> 00:04:30,040
I've taken Winterfell.

46
00:04:30,930 --> 00:04:33,750
And I will keep Winterfell.

47
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:38,270
Leave us.

48
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:53,750
Theon, you're my blood.

49
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:57,220
We both loved our mother.

50
00:04:57,430 --> 00:05:00,760
We both endured our father.

51
00:05:02,410 --> 00:05:04,780
Come home with me. Don't die here alone.

52
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:06,540
I don't intend to die.

53
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:14,430
You were a terrible baby, do you know that?

54
00:05:16,180 --> 00:05:18,670
Bawling all the time, never sleeping.

55
00:05:20,410 --> 00:05:22,810
And one night you just wouldn't shut up,

56
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:25,380
screaming like a dying pig.

57
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,410
I walked over to your crib, I looked down at you.

58
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,720
I wanted to strangle you.

59
00:05:33,990 --> 00:05:36,850
And you looked up at me and you stopped screaming.

60
00:05:38,410 --> 00:05:40,090
You smiled at me.

61
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:47,640
Don't die so far from the sea.

62
00:06:02,390 --> 00:06:05,390
I've brought you a present, Lord of Bones.

63
00:06:06,570 --> 00:06:09,510
I already got one crow. Don't need two.

64
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:11,650
Mance will want to question this one.

65
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:14,490
Knows all about where the crows are and what they're planning.

66
00:06:14,490 --> 00:06:18,330
The Halfhand knows more. This one is just a little boy.

67
00:06:18,550 --> 00:06:19,580
Gut him.

68
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:22,330
He could have killed me half a dozen times.

69
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:25,410
And now he wishes he did. Gut him.

70
00:06:25,410 --> 00:06:29,010
He's a bastard of Winterfell, Ned Stark's son.

71
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:34,190
Mance will want him.

72
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:37,720
What does Mance want with a dead man's bastard?

73
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:39,120
I don't know.

74
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:41,860
I think he'll want to decide for himself.

75
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:52,260
He runs, I'll chop his balls off.

76
00:06:52,260 --> 00:06:55,310
He runs, I'll do it meself.

77
00:07:02,370 --> 00:07:05,020
We're even now, Jon Snow.

78
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:19,710
I couldn't do it.

79
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:22,180
I had the sword at her neck, I just couldn't--

80
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:25,310
- I know. - The others?

81
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:27,960
When you didn't come back, we went looking for you.

82
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:30,560
We found your tracks fast enough.

83
00:07:31,070 --> 00:07:33,630
But they found us before we found you.

84
00:07:35,130 --> 00:07:36,920
They died because of me.

85
00:07:38,030 --> 00:07:39,810
See that it wasn't for nothing.

86
00:07:39,810 --> 00:07:41,250
All right, up, lad.

87
00:07:41,250 --> 00:07:43,060
Come on, on your feet, now.

88
00:07:43,130 --> 00:07:44,100
Move it.

89
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,370
Is she beautiful?

90
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:54,910
I've never met her.

91
00:07:55,870 --> 00:07:57,210
What's her name?

92
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:59,310
Frey, I suppose.

93
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:00,990
I don't know her first name.

94
00:08:01,970 --> 00:08:03,960
I'm sure you'll be very happy.

95
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,930
And you're marrying her for a bridge?

96
00:08:09,930 --> 00:08:12,190
An important bridge.

97
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:15,580
It was before they killed my father.

98
00:08:16,690 --> 00:08:19,510
I still thought I could march south and rescue him in time,

99
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:21,360
but only if I crossed that bridge.

100
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,080
When I speak to people from the North,

101
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,230
they all loved your father.

102
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,860
He was the best man I ever met.

103
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:35,270
I know children always think that about their fathers, but--

104
00:08:35,270 --> 00:08:37,980
Children do not always think that about their fathers,

105
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:39,430
believe me.

106
00:08:41,010 --> 00:08:44,160
He once told me that being a Lord is like being a father,

107
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:46,960
except you have thousands of children

108
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:49,050
and you worry about all of them.

109
00:08:49,450 --> 00:08:52,370
The farmers plowing the fields are yours to protect.

110
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:55,610
The charwomen scrubbing the floors, yours to protect.

111
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,730
The soldiers you order into battle.

112
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:01,690
He told me he woke with fear in the morning

113
00:09:01,690 --> 00:09:03,600
and went to bed with fear in the night.

114
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:07,300
I didn't believe him.

115
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,750
I asked him,

116
00:09:11,010 --> 00:09:13,430
"How can a man be brave if he's afraid?"

117
00:09:14,530 --> 00:09:17,580
"That is the only time a man can be brave," He told me.

118
00:09:21,210 --> 00:09:22,900
I wish I could have met him.

119
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:26,080
He would have liked you.

120
00:09:28,930 --> 00:09:30,880
Most Lords worry more about their gold

121
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:33,480
and their glory than the charwomen scrubbing their floors.

122
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:35,820
He didn't care much about gold or glory.

123
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:37,120
And you?

124
00:09:37,270 --> 00:09:40,200
You think I'm fighting this war so they'll sing songs about me?

125
00:09:41,890 --> 00:09:43,440
I want to go home.

126
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:46,670
I want the men following me to go home.

127
00:09:46,670 --> 00:09:48,010
Then why don't you?

128
00:09:48,010 --> 00:09:51,090
Because we'll never be safe until the Lannisters are defeated.

129
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:53,870
And because I believe in justice.

130
00:09:53,870 --> 00:09:56,040
Chopping off Joffrey's head, you mean.

131
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:57,780
That would be a start.

132
00:10:07,410 --> 00:10:09,370
Your Grace, Milady.

133
00:10:09,750 --> 00:10:12,610
The Kingslayer, he escaped in the night.

134
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:14,210
How?

135
00:10:16,090 --> 00:10:17,280
How?!

136
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:23,850
Tell me this isn't true.

137
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:29,820
Why?

138
00:10:31,610 --> 00:10:34,250
- For the girls. - You betrayed me.

139
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:35,670
- Robb... - No!

140
00:10:36,180 --> 00:10:39,520
You knew I would not allow it and you did it anyway.

141
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:44,040
Bran and Rickon are captives in Winterfell.

142
00:10:44,070 --> 00:10:47,050
Sansa and Arya are captives in King's Landing.

143
00:10:47,190 --> 00:10:50,020
I have five children, and only one of them is free.

144
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:53,630
I lost one son fighting by your son's side.

145
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:57,350
I lost another to the Kingslayer, strangled with a chain.

146
00:10:58,180 --> 00:11:02,760
You commit treason because your children are prisoners?

147
00:11:02,990 --> 00:11:06,860
I would carve out my heart and offer it to the father if he would

148
00:11:06,890 --> 00:11:11,380
let my sons wake from their graves and step into a prison cell.

149
00:11:11,380 --> 00:11:13,030
I grieve for your sons, My Lord.

150
00:11:13,030 --> 00:11:15,600
I don't want your grief. I want my vengeance.

151
00:11:15,930 --> 00:11:18,280
And you stole it from me.

152
00:11:19,870 --> 00:11:23,170
Killing Jaime Lannister would not buy life for your children,

153
00:11:23,670 --> 00:11:27,340
but returning him to King's Landing may buy life for mine.

154
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:31,480
Jaime Lannister has played you for a fool.

155
00:11:31,950 --> 00:11:33,970
You've weakened our position.

156
00:11:34,150 --> 00:11:36,420
You've brought discord into our camp.

157
00:11:36,810 --> 00:11:39,040
And you did it all behind my back.

158
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:44,830
Make sure she's guarded day and night.

159
00:11:44,830 --> 00:11:45,550
Robb.

160
00:11:45,550 --> 00:11:47,780
How many men did we send in pursuit of the Kingslayer?

161
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:49,100
40, Your Grace.

162
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:52,240
Send another 40 with our fastest horses.

163
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:53,350
Robb.

164
00:12:11,420 --> 00:12:12,580
Damn.

165
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:18,210
You're much uglier in daylight.

166
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:19,960
What's your name?

167
00:12:21,330 --> 00:12:23,890
I'm Jaime Lannister of Casterly Rock,

168
00:12:23,890 --> 00:12:25,540
son of Tywin.

169
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:30,310
A captive knight has a right to know his captor's identity.

170
00:12:30,820 --> 00:12:32,210
Brienne of Tarth.

171
00:12:32,210 --> 00:12:34,360
Tarth, Tarth, Tarth.

172
00:12:34,370 --> 00:12:36,990
Crescent moons and starbursts.

173
00:12:36,990 --> 00:12:41,060
Lord... Selwyn Tarth,

174
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:42,550
your father.

175
00:12:43,610 --> 00:12:46,260
Do you have any brothers and sisters, My Lady?

176
00:12:47,010 --> 00:12:49,440
It's a long way to King's Landing.

177
00:12:49,830 --> 00:12:52,150
Might as well get to know one another.

178
00:12:52,810 --> 00:12:54,360
Have you known many men?

179
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:55,810
I suppose not.

180
00:12:55,810 --> 00:12:57,090
Women?

181
00:12:57,520 --> 00:12:58,750
Horses?

182
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,150
I didn't mean to give offense, My Lady.

183
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:03,110
Forgive me.

184
00:13:03,110 --> 00:13:05,580
Your crimes are past forgiveness, Kingslayer.

185
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:07,070
Why do you hate me so much?

186
00:13:07,070 --> 00:13:09,740
- Have I ever harmed you? - You've harmed others...

187
00:13:10,010 --> 00:13:12,210
those you were sworn to protect,

188
00:13:12,450 --> 00:13:14,430
the weak, the innocent.

189
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:17,680
Has anyone ever told you you're as boring as you are ugly?

190
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:20,170
You will not provoke me to anger.

191
00:13:20,170 --> 00:13:22,620
I already have. Look at you.

192
00:13:22,890 --> 00:13:24,820
You're ready to chop my head off.

193
00:13:25,470 --> 00:13:27,080
Do you think you could?

194
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:29,340
Do you think you could beat me in a fair fight?

195
00:13:29,340 --> 00:13:31,060
I've never seen you fight.

196
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:33,050
The answer is no.

197
00:13:33,450 --> 00:13:36,620
There are three men in the kingdoms who might have a chance against me.

198
00:13:36,620 --> 00:13:38,340
You're not one of them.

199
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:41,280
All my life men like you have sneered at me.

200
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:44,600
And all my life I've been knocking men like you into the dust.

201
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:47,080
If you're so confident, unlock my chains.

202
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,600
Let's see what happens.

203
00:13:48,850 --> 00:13:51,770
Do you take me for an idiot? In.

204
00:13:54,290 --> 00:13:57,040
I took you for a fighter,

205
00:13:57,040 --> 00:14:00,840
a man-- pardon-- woman of honor.

206
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:02,990
Was I wrong?

207
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:04,980
You're afraid.

208
00:14:06,950 --> 00:14:10,090
Maybe one day we'll find out, Kingslayer.

209
00:14:23,410 --> 00:14:27,380
King's Landing will fall an hour after Stannis lands his force.

210
00:14:28,750 --> 00:14:31,120
It's not too late for King Joffrey and Cersei

211
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:33,490
and the court to ride west to safety.

212
00:14:34,490 --> 00:14:36,280
Surrender the Iron Throne?

213
00:14:36,290 --> 00:14:39,400
Better than seeing their heads mounted on the city gates.

214
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:41,870
Stannis will execute them all.

215
00:14:41,870 --> 00:14:44,810
No, a king who runs will not be king for long.

216
00:14:45,230 --> 00:14:47,890
He's a Lannister. He'll stand and fight.

217
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:51,850
Stannis, two days from the capital

218
00:14:52,190 --> 00:14:53,940
and the wolf at my doorstep.

219
00:14:53,940 --> 00:14:57,150
The scouts assure us Robb Stark remains north of Ashemark.

220
00:14:57,450 --> 00:14:59,760
The last time the scouts assured us

221
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:02,660
of Stark's movement, he lured us into a trap.

222
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:06,960
Which is why my son is his prisoner.

223
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:12,870
Too close to Casterly Rock.

224
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:17,640
He sent a splinter force to recapture Winterfell.

225
00:15:18,070 --> 00:15:20,300
The Greyjoys have done us a great favor.

226
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:24,990
Stark won't risk marching on Casterly Rock until he's at full force.

227
00:15:24,990 --> 00:15:27,530
He's a boy and he's never lost a battle.

228
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:31,260
He'll risk anything at any time

229
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:34,630
because he doesn't know enough to be afraid.

230
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:44,190
We'll ride at nightfall.

231
00:15:44,260 --> 00:15:47,420
I want a full night's march before he knows we're on the move.

232
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:50,980
Clegane, you'll maintain a Garrison here at Harrenhal.

233
00:15:51,270 --> 00:15:54,480
Track down this brotherhood and destroy them.

234
00:15:56,970 --> 00:15:59,250
The girl has proven herself a good servant.

235
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:01,480
She'll stay on with you.

236
00:16:02,150 --> 00:16:04,910
See that he doesn't get drunk in the evenings.

237
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:07,160
He's poor company when he's sober,

238
00:16:07,410 --> 00:16:09,520
but he's better at his work.

239
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:18,860
You've got some questions to answer.

240
00:16:19,380 --> 00:16:21,290
Who killed Ser Amory?

241
00:16:21,290 --> 00:16:23,320
- I don't know! - Give me the name.

242
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:25,330
- Please! - Take this one out for the crows.

243
00:16:25,330 --> 00:16:28,310
I told you, I don't know.

244
00:16:28,650 --> 00:16:29,960
Please.

245
00:16:30,810 --> 00:16:33,610
Look, it's Yoren's little cunt.

246
00:16:33,610 --> 00:16:35,800
Used to be a boy, now it's a girl.

247
00:16:36,540 --> 00:16:37,910
Where's Jaqen?

248
00:16:37,910 --> 00:16:39,510
Don't care.

249
00:16:40,250 --> 00:16:42,720
Where's your stick now, bitch?

250
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:44,580
I promised to fuck you with it.

251
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:47,580
Come on, time to kill some wolves.

252
00:16:56,810 --> 00:16:58,910
You need sour cherries to make it right.

253
00:16:58,910 --> 00:17:00,770
And the secret is you dry the stones,

254
00:17:00,780 --> 00:17:02,270
and then you break them with a mallet.

255
00:17:02,270 --> 00:17:03,910
That's where the real flavor is.

256
00:17:03,910 --> 00:17:05,480
You crush 'em up real fine.

257
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:06,720
And then when you're finished,

258
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:07,640
you sprinkle them over the piecrust.

259
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:09,610
- Where's Jaqen? - How would I know?

260
00:17:09,610 --> 00:17:11,080
I need him now.

261
00:17:11,590 --> 00:17:13,180
Lord Tywin's marching tonight.

262
00:17:13,180 --> 00:17:15,920
- You need him? - He's helping me.

263
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:18,490
- I saw him. - Where?

264
00:17:21,350 --> 00:17:22,450
Where?!

265
00:17:22,450 --> 00:17:23,180
Where?

266
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:25,300
They went riding out the gates a few hours ago.

267
00:17:25,610 --> 00:17:28,490
On patrol. Let go of my ears.

268
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:35,250
What do you want with him anyway?

269
00:17:51,210 --> 00:17:53,130
Mance is gonna march on the Wall.

270
00:17:53,130 --> 00:17:55,850
When he does, one brother inside his army

271
00:17:55,850 --> 00:17:57,760
will be worth 1,000 fighting against it.

272
00:17:57,760 --> 00:17:59,850
- They'll never trust me. - They might...

273
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,800
- If you do what needs to be done. - What?

274
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:04,430
How does it feel knowing those men all died

275
00:18:04,430 --> 00:18:07,630
so you could skip through the snow with your little savage girl?

276
00:18:07,630 --> 00:18:08,150
I didn't.

277
00:18:08,150 --> 00:18:11,730
I should have known better, trusting a traitor's bastard.

278
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:18,720
He's not yours to kill, crow.

279
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:43,170
Do you have to do that here?

280
00:18:44,650 --> 00:18:46,630
I like to keep me hands clean.

281
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:50,150
Yes, but do you have to do it here?

282
00:18:59,580 --> 00:19:01,100
You should start wearing the gold cloak.

283
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:02,580
I don't want to wear a gold cloak.

284
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:04,640
You're commander of the City Watch.

285
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:06,380
You shouldn't be dressed like a common sellsword.

286
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:08,210
A cloak slows you down in a fight,

287
00:19:08,250 --> 00:19:10,370
makes it hard to move quietly.

288
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:12,320
And the gold catches the light,

289
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:14,290
so you're nice and easy to spot at night.

290
00:19:14,290 --> 00:19:17,100
Well, you're not sneaking through alleyways any longer.

291
00:19:17,500 --> 00:19:19,020
You're supposed to stand out.

292
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:22,150
We had a deal, and wearing a gold cloak wasn't part of it.

293
00:19:22,150 --> 00:19:24,030
Fine, fine.

294
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:27,470
No gold cloak.

295
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:37,350
- What? - What?

296
00:19:37,350 --> 00:19:39,930
What? What? Why are you staring at me?

297
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,500
You don't want me cleaning me nails.

298
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:44,280
You don't want me looking your way.

299
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:45,930
Why am I here?

300
00:19:46,050 --> 00:19:49,300
To help me plan the defense of King's Landing.

301
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:51,290
Stannis will be here any day.

302
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:57,500
And one of these explains how to beat him?

303
00:19:59,330 --> 00:20:01,740
"A History of the Great Sieges of Westeros"

304
00:20:01,740 --> 00:20:04,460
by Archmaester "Shevelathin."

305
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:06,720
"Shevelatesh."

306
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:08,450
"Chevalteesh."

307
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:14,300
I'd swap all your books for a few good archers.

308
00:20:14,470 --> 00:20:16,590
My Lord Hand, Commander.

309
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:18,550
I must compliment you

310
00:20:18,550 --> 00:20:21,760
on the Gold Cloaks' performance these last few weeks.

311
00:20:22,110 --> 00:20:25,310
Did you know there has been a marked drop in thievery?

312
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,430
I did not know.

313
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:32,330
And how did you accomplish this marked drop in thievery?

314
00:20:32,610 --> 00:20:35,150
Me and the lads rounded up all the known thieves.

315
00:20:36,290 --> 00:20:37,790
For questioning?

316
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,230
Uh, no.

317
00:20:40,410 --> 00:20:42,850
It's just the unknown thieves we need to worry about now.

318
00:20:42,850 --> 00:20:45,020
- We talked about this. - Aye, we talked about it.

319
00:20:45,670 --> 00:20:47,920
Have you ever been in a city under siege?

320
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:50,950
Maybe this part's not in your books.

321
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:53,610
See, it's not the fighting that kills most people.

322
00:20:53,610 --> 00:20:56,700
It's the starving. Food's worth more than gold.

323
00:20:57,150 --> 00:21:00,360
Noble ladies sell their diamonds for a sack of potatoes.

324
00:21:00,870 --> 00:21:02,480
Things get bad enough,

325
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:04,590
the poor start eating each other.

326
00:21:04,980 --> 00:21:07,360
The thieves, they love a siege.

327
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:10,450
Soon as the gates are sealed, they steal all the food.

328
00:21:10,450 --> 00:21:13,790
By the time it's all over, they're the richest men in town.

329
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:16,880
Given the circumstances, My Lord,

330
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:20,190
I believe extreme measures are warranted.

331
00:21:22,370 --> 00:21:25,260
"The Great Sieges of Westeros."

332
00:21:25,260 --> 00:21:27,140
Thrilling subject.

333
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:31,890
Shame Archmaester Ch'vyalthan wasn't a better writer.

334
00:21:36,180 --> 00:21:38,340
Stannis knows King's Landing.

335
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:41,850
He knows where the walls are strongest

336
00:21:41,850 --> 00:21:45,610
and he knows which gates are weakest.

337
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:49,900
The Mud Gate.

338
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:53,400
A good ram will batter it down in minutes

339
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:55,630
and it's only 50 yards from the water.

340
00:21:55,630 --> 00:21:57,400
That's where he'll land.

341
00:21:57,400 --> 00:22:00,240
And if Stannis does attack the Mud Gate,

342
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:02,040
what is our plan?

343
00:22:02,970 --> 00:22:04,700
We could throw books at his men.

344
00:22:04,700 --> 00:22:06,330
We don't have that many books.

345
00:22:06,340 --> 00:22:08,200
We don't have that many men, either.

346
00:22:08,860 --> 00:22:10,730
What do we have?

347
00:22:12,260 --> 00:22:14,140
Pig shit.

348
00:22:32,390 --> 00:22:34,600
I'm not cut out for this sort of work.

349
00:22:35,030 --> 00:22:38,030
I always imagined meself doing something much worse.

350
00:22:38,450 --> 00:22:41,140
We're digging latrine pits at the end of the world.

351
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:43,690
I can't imagine anything much worse.

352
00:22:44,160 --> 00:22:46,270
You lack imagination.

353
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:50,630
Where do you think Jon is right now?

354
00:22:50,670 --> 00:22:53,770
He went off with the Halfhand. He didn't come back.

355
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:56,160
A betting man would go with dead.

356
00:22:57,030 --> 00:22:58,530
He's not dead.

357
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:01,140
No, Jon's a great fighter.

358
00:23:01,140 --> 00:23:02,740
Well, he's better than me

359
00:23:03,110 --> 00:23:04,830
and a lot better than you.

360
00:23:04,840 --> 00:23:07,550
He's got a Valyrian steel sword.

361
00:23:08,040 --> 00:23:09,840
So did his father.

362
00:23:10,030 --> 00:23:12,620
And Qhorin Halfhand is the greatest ranger alive.

363
00:23:12,620 --> 00:23:15,350
Great rangers never get old is the problem.

364
00:23:15,420 --> 00:23:16,970
Shit ones neither.

365
00:23:18,180 --> 00:23:20,880
It's them in the middle that last a long time.

366
00:23:26,370 --> 00:23:28,310
What in seven hells is that?

367
00:23:44,500 --> 00:23:46,360
The First Men made these marks.

368
00:23:46,740 --> 00:23:48,250
Help me with it.

369
00:24:02,030 --> 00:24:03,200
Look.

370
00:24:07,440 --> 00:24:09,700
If you find something you're not supposed to,

371
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:13,120
best thing to do is pretend you've never seen it.

372
00:24:13,120 --> 00:24:14,760
That's a Night's Watch cloak.

373
00:24:15,040 --> 00:24:16,710
It's been here a long time.

374
00:24:22,270 --> 00:24:25,240
Oh, must be Dragonglass.

375
00:24:25,330 --> 00:24:26,860
Dragonglass?

376
00:24:27,160 --> 00:24:28,990
The Maesters call it Obsidian.

377
00:24:31,620 --> 00:24:33,400
Why would a brother hide it here?

378
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:36,360
I expect it's 'cause he wanted somebody to find it.

379
00:24:42,500 --> 00:24:44,080
Mind where you're going.

380
00:24:52,920 --> 00:24:54,840
I'm sorry. I'll--

381
00:24:55,870 --> 00:24:59,070
- Where were you? - A man has patrol duty.

382
00:24:59,070 --> 00:25:01,990
Tywin Lannister was right here and now he's gone.

383
00:25:01,990 --> 00:25:03,830
A girl owes one more name.

384
00:25:03,830 --> 00:25:06,590
The Red God demands it. Give the man a name.

385
00:25:07,630 --> 00:25:09,330
How long after I give you the name

386
00:25:09,330 --> 00:25:11,190
does it take you to kill someone?

387
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:14,980
A minute, an hour, a month.

388
00:25:16,140 --> 00:25:20,330
Death is certain, the time is not.

389
00:25:20,330 --> 00:25:22,420
He's taking his army to attack my brother.

390
00:25:22,620 --> 00:25:24,540
I need him dead right now.

391
00:25:25,380 --> 00:25:27,140
This a man cannot do.

392
00:25:28,620 --> 00:25:30,190
You promised you'd help me.

393
00:25:30,190 --> 00:25:32,340
Help was not promised, lovely girl.

394
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:35,310
Only death. There must be others.

395
00:25:35,310 --> 00:25:37,070
Give a name, any name.

396
00:25:37,410 --> 00:25:39,000
And you'll kill them?

397
00:25:40,090 --> 00:25:41,500
Anybody?

398
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:47,650
By the seven New Gods and the Old Gods beyond counting,

399
00:25:47,650 --> 00:25:49,070
I swear it.

400
00:25:52,200 --> 00:25:53,380
All right.

401
00:25:59,150 --> 00:26:00,760
Jaqen H'ghar.

402
00:26:07,580 --> 00:26:09,720
A girl gives a man his own name?

403
00:26:09,730 --> 00:26:12,250
- That's right. - Gods are not mocked.

404
00:26:12,250 --> 00:26:14,710
- This is no joking thing. - I'm not joking.

405
00:26:14,710 --> 00:26:16,210
A man can go kill himself.

406
00:26:16,210 --> 00:26:18,340
- Un-name me. - No.

407
00:26:18,350 --> 00:26:19,700
Please?

408
00:26:22,100 --> 00:26:23,530
I'll un-name you.

409
00:26:24,650 --> 00:26:25,510
Thank you.

410
00:26:25,510 --> 00:26:27,650
If you help me and my friends escape.

411
00:26:29,290 --> 00:26:30,900
This would require more than one life.

412
00:26:30,900 --> 00:26:34,110
- This is not part of our bargain. - Fine, Jaqen H'ghar.

413
00:26:34,660 --> 00:26:36,360
A girl lacks honor.

414
00:26:44,120 --> 00:26:47,070
If I do this thing, a girl must obey.

415
00:26:47,070 --> 00:26:48,760
A girl will obey.

416
00:26:50,940 --> 00:26:53,930
A girl and her friends will walk through the gate at midnight.

417
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:00,770
Thank you, Podrick.

418
00:27:07,550 --> 00:27:09,040
Odd little boy.

419
00:27:09,700 --> 00:27:12,290
I have a certain sympathy for odd little boys.

420
00:27:12,480 --> 00:27:14,070
You and Varys both.

421
00:27:16,120 --> 00:27:17,900
Excellent lamprey pie.

422
00:27:18,330 --> 00:27:20,870
Were you slaving away in the kitchen all day?

423
00:27:22,090 --> 00:27:24,320
I hear Joffrey plans on fighting.

424
00:27:24,340 --> 00:27:26,240
An inspiration for the troops.

425
00:27:26,240 --> 00:27:28,110
The young king in his shining armor

426
00:27:28,110 --> 00:27:30,820
fighting to defend the capital against the wicked old rebel.

427
00:27:30,820 --> 00:27:32,280
He's only a boy.

428
00:27:32,490 --> 00:27:34,850
Younger boys are off fighting his war.

429
00:27:35,830 --> 00:27:37,050
He's not ready.

430
00:27:37,050 --> 00:27:38,950
What is he, 17?

431
00:27:39,260 --> 00:27:42,120
- Remember Jaime at 17? - Better than you.

432
00:27:42,290 --> 00:27:44,920
Some men have a gift for this sort of thing,

433
00:27:44,980 --> 00:27:46,590
some don't.

434
00:27:46,990 --> 00:27:48,910
His place is not on the battlefield.

435
00:27:48,910 --> 00:27:50,860
It's not on the throne, either,

436
00:27:50,920 --> 00:27:52,830
sadly for all of us.

437
00:27:56,560 --> 00:27:58,250
Do you think I'm an idiot?

438
00:27:58,260 --> 00:28:00,550
No, I'd say you possess above average intelligence.

439
00:28:00,550 --> 00:28:02,760
You shipped off my only daughter.

440
00:28:02,870 --> 00:28:06,220
And now you want to send my eldest son to the battlefield to die.

441
00:28:06,220 --> 00:28:08,290
He'll have his Kingsguard protecting him.

442
00:28:08,450 --> 00:28:10,880
He has the finest armor gold can buy.

443
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:13,210
He needs to be out there.

444
00:28:13,210 --> 00:28:15,320
The men will fight more fiercely seeing their king

445
00:28:15,330 --> 00:28:16,770
fighting beside them

446
00:28:16,770 --> 00:28:19,660
instead of hiding behind his mother's skirts.

447
00:28:20,460 --> 00:28:21,650
Any dessert?

448
00:28:22,550 --> 00:28:24,640
Do you know why Varys is so dangerous?

449
00:28:25,390 --> 00:28:28,110
Because he has thousands of spies in his employ.

450
00:28:28,720 --> 00:28:31,670
Because he knows everything we do before we do it.

451
00:28:31,670 --> 00:28:33,330
Because he doesn't have a cock.

452
00:28:33,860 --> 00:28:35,280
Neither do you.

453
00:28:37,010 --> 00:28:38,810
Perhaps I'm dangerous, too.

454
00:28:39,570 --> 00:28:40,930
You, on the other hand,

455
00:28:41,470 --> 00:28:43,270
are as big a fool as every other man.

456
00:28:44,020 --> 00:28:47,630
That little worm between your legs does half your thinking.

457
00:28:47,630 --> 00:28:48,970
It's not that little.

458
00:28:56,230 --> 00:28:57,580
Why are you smiling?

459
00:28:58,180 --> 00:28:59,620
Because I'm happy.

460
00:29:00,020 --> 00:29:01,080
And why are you happy?

461
00:29:05,800 --> 00:29:07,670
Because I have your little whore.

462
00:29:11,540 --> 00:29:13,250
I thought you preferred blondes.

463
00:29:13,470 --> 00:29:14,960
Such a droll little fellow.

464
00:29:15,440 --> 00:29:17,430
Tell me, have you married this one yet?

465
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:18,610
No?

466
00:29:19,550 --> 00:29:21,800
Oh, good. Father will be so pleased.

467
00:29:22,160 --> 00:29:23,700
Why do you care who I fuck?

468
00:29:24,150 --> 00:29:26,350
Because a Lannister always pays her debts.

469
00:29:26,860 --> 00:29:28,460
You stole my only daughter,

470
00:29:28,650 --> 00:29:30,270
you plot to have Joffrey killed.

471
00:29:30,270 --> 00:29:33,140
This is madness. Stannis will be here in days.

472
00:29:33,140 --> 00:29:34,510
- You need me. - For what?

473
00:29:34,510 --> 00:29:35,960
Your skill in battle?

474
00:29:38,380 --> 00:29:40,470
Pretty thing, your whore.

475
00:29:41,340 --> 00:29:42,610
Lovely body.

476
00:29:43,320 --> 00:29:45,300
The bruises will heal in time.

477
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:48,610
Where did you find her?

478
00:29:48,970 --> 00:29:51,420
Varys isn't the only one who hears whispers.

479
00:29:51,620 --> 00:29:53,970
Really, a Lannister lion necklace?

480
00:29:55,150 --> 00:29:57,760
You need to hide your secret whores more carefully.

481
00:29:57,940 --> 00:30:00,600
You've forgotten the most important thing about whores.

482
00:30:00,660 --> 00:30:01,290
Oh?

483
00:30:02,800 --> 00:30:04,930
Well, you're the expert. Tell me.

484
00:30:06,590 --> 00:30:08,130
You don't buy them.

485
00:30:08,450 --> 00:30:09,670
You only rent them.

486
00:30:11,120 --> 00:30:13,310
You're usually a better liar, baby brother.

487
00:30:14,830 --> 00:30:16,030
This one you like.

488
00:30:17,510 --> 00:30:18,980
You like her very much.

489
00:30:20,640 --> 00:30:21,860
Could it be love?

490
00:30:23,020 --> 00:30:25,360
Don't worry, she'll be treated gently enough...

491
00:30:25,850 --> 00:30:27,460
unless Joffrey is hurt.

492
00:30:27,460 --> 00:30:30,120
And then every wound he suffers she'll suffer, too.

493
00:30:31,160 --> 00:30:32,530
And if he dies,

494
00:30:33,660 --> 00:30:35,510
there isn't a man alive who could devise

495
00:30:35,510 --> 00:30:38,440
a more painful death for your little cunt.

496
00:30:41,620 --> 00:30:44,830
And how do I know you haven't killed her already?

497
00:30:45,120 --> 00:30:46,420
Would you like to see her?

498
00:30:46,420 --> 00:30:47,710
I thought you might.

499
00:30:48,150 --> 00:30:50,560
Ser Mandon, bring in my brother's whore.

500
00:31:23,320 --> 00:31:24,800
I'm sorry they hurt you.

501
00:31:26,820 --> 00:31:28,570
You must be brave.

502
00:31:34,050 --> 00:31:36,860
I promise I will free you.

503
00:31:38,370 --> 00:31:39,710
Don't forget me.

504
00:31:40,370 --> 00:31:41,430
Never.

505
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:01,950
I will hurt you for this.

506
00:32:02,670 --> 00:32:06,260
A day will come when you think you're safe and happy

507
00:32:06,260 --> 00:32:10,260
and your joy will turn to ashes in your mouth.

508
00:32:11,410 --> 00:32:13,390
And you will know the debt is paid.

509
00:32:13,970 --> 00:32:16,040
Get out.

510
00:32:27,610 --> 00:32:28,410
Shae!

511
00:32:32,250 --> 00:32:33,910
I've been waiting all night.

512
00:32:34,740 --> 00:32:35,850
What is wrong?

513
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:38,420
You're beautiful.

514
00:32:46,310 --> 00:32:47,900
Then why do you look sad?

515
00:32:55,220 --> 00:32:56,900
We have to be more careful.

516
00:32:57,080 --> 00:33:00,350
Don't be afraid. I can take care of myself.

517
00:33:00,740 --> 00:33:02,870
There are people who want to hurt me.

518
00:33:03,630 --> 00:33:05,890
I know. I won't let them.

519
00:33:05,960 --> 00:33:08,380
I'll cut off their faces. I will.

520
00:33:13,180 --> 00:33:16,010
I would kill for you. Do you know that?

521
00:33:16,970 --> 00:33:20,280
I expect I'll have to before this is over.

522
00:33:23,190 --> 00:33:24,360
You're mine.

523
00:33:26,260 --> 00:33:27,390
I'm yours.

524
00:33:28,940 --> 00:33:30,110
Promise me.

525
00:33:34,150 --> 00:33:36,680
I'm yours, and you are mine.

526
00:33:48,750 --> 00:33:50,390
Still no word?

527
00:33:51,100 --> 00:33:52,950
We've sent a dozen ravens.

528
00:33:53,250 --> 00:33:54,480
None have returned.

529
00:33:56,040 --> 00:33:58,970
My bastard is only a few days from Winterfell.

530
00:33:59,190 --> 00:34:01,290
- Once he captures the castle-- - Theon has my brothers.

531
00:34:01,290 --> 00:34:02,390
If we storm the castle...

532
00:34:02,390 --> 00:34:04,620
He wouldn't dare hurt the boys.

533
00:34:06,360 --> 00:34:09,360
They're his only hope of escaping the North with his head.

534
00:34:11,470 --> 00:34:13,140
Send word to your son.

535
00:34:14,740 --> 00:34:16,310
Any Ironborn who surrender

536
00:34:16,310 --> 00:34:19,190
will be allowed to return safely to their homes.

537
00:34:20,150 --> 00:34:22,710
A touch of mercy is a virtue, Your Grace.

538
00:34:22,710 --> 00:34:26,730
- Too much-- - Any Ironborn with the exception of Theon Greyjoy.

539
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:29,680
He betrayed our cause.

540
00:34:30,280 --> 00:34:31,610
He betrayed me.

541
00:34:32,730 --> 00:34:35,320
And we will hunt him down no matter where he runs.

542
00:34:35,990 --> 00:34:39,080
I expect his countrymen will turn on him the minute they hear the offer.

543
00:34:42,070 --> 00:34:43,460
Your pardon, My Lord.

544
00:34:43,970 --> 00:34:44,850
Your Grace.

545
00:34:44,850 --> 00:34:45,830
My Lady.

546
00:34:58,300 --> 00:34:59,380
How are you?

547
00:35:01,410 --> 00:35:02,610
How am I?

548
00:35:03,160 --> 00:35:04,780
I've had to arrest my mother.

549
00:35:05,390 --> 00:35:07,230
The Lannisters have my sisters.

550
00:35:07,430 --> 00:35:10,040
The man I considered my closest friend

551
00:35:10,330 --> 00:35:12,470
has seized my home and my brothers.

552
00:35:12,620 --> 00:35:15,670
I'm fighting a war and I don't know if I should march south or north.

553
00:35:15,670 --> 00:35:18,040
I'm sorry. It was a stupid question.

554
00:35:18,040 --> 00:35:19,870
- I'm sorry. - No.

555
00:35:20,290 --> 00:35:21,330
Forgive me.

556
00:35:22,480 --> 00:35:24,880
You're being kind. I have no right...

557
00:35:24,880 --> 00:35:26,130
You have every right.

558
00:35:26,780 --> 00:35:27,900
You're a king.

559
00:35:28,290 --> 00:35:30,280
That's not the kind of king I want to be.

560
00:35:31,300 --> 00:35:32,910
What kind do you want to be?

561
00:35:33,130 --> 00:35:34,050
I don't know.

562
00:35:34,050 --> 00:35:35,220
The good kind.

563
00:35:39,460 --> 00:35:41,300
Most kings grew up as princes.

564
00:35:41,300 --> 00:35:44,320
They spend their whole lives preparing for the crown.

565
00:35:44,690 --> 00:35:46,700
I was raised to be Lord of Winterfell.

566
00:35:49,450 --> 00:35:51,650
I was raised to be a proper little lady,

567
00:35:51,880 --> 00:35:54,980
to play the harp and dance the latest steps

568
00:35:54,980 --> 00:35:57,240
and recite Valyrian poetry.

569
00:35:57,390 --> 00:35:58,800
I'd like to hear you play the harp.

570
00:35:58,800 --> 00:36:00,510
No. No, you would not.

571
00:36:05,970 --> 00:36:09,510
How did you go from reciting Valyrian poetry

572
00:36:09,860 --> 00:36:11,610
to sawing off men's feet?

573
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:23,840
When I was 12,

574
00:36:24,270 --> 00:36:26,280
my mother and father went to a wedding.

575
00:36:26,980 --> 00:36:29,610
Weddings in Volantis last for days, you know.

576
00:36:30,320 --> 00:36:32,090
And they left me with my little brother.

577
00:36:33,880 --> 00:36:35,690
The second afternoon they were gone

578
00:36:35,690 --> 00:36:38,730
was the hottest day in the three-year summer.

579
00:36:39,060 --> 00:36:42,210
We couldn't bear to be inside, so we ran down to the Rhoyne.

580
00:36:43,060 --> 00:36:46,010
Every child in Volantis was in the Rhoyne that day.

581
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:49,630
The rich, the poor, we were all there,

582
00:36:49,810 --> 00:36:53,080
naked, screaming, racing to the little islands.

583
00:36:53,400 --> 00:36:55,900
Drummers were playing for coppers on the east bank.

584
00:37:00,510 --> 00:37:02,000
I was treading water,

585
00:37:03,250 --> 00:37:04,560
talking to a friend

586
00:37:05,440 --> 00:37:07,450
when I realized I hadn't seen my brother.

587
00:37:09,370 --> 00:37:10,550
I called his name.

588
00:37:12,380 --> 00:37:14,490
Then I started screaming his name.

589
00:37:16,960 --> 00:37:18,180
And then I saw him

590
00:37:19,400 --> 00:37:20,760
floating facedown.

591
00:37:23,150 --> 00:37:26,050
My heart just... stopped.

592
00:37:26,050 --> 00:37:26,750
I was...

593
00:37:31,380 --> 00:37:33,490
I dragged him from the water.

594
00:37:34,730 --> 00:37:36,570
My friend helped me, I think.

595
00:37:36,840 --> 00:37:38,280
I don't even remember.

596
00:37:41,520 --> 00:37:42,630
He was so little.

597
00:37:44,640 --> 00:37:46,770
Then we pulled him onto the riverbank...

598
00:37:48,930 --> 00:37:50,980
and I screamed at him

599
00:37:51,250 --> 00:37:52,510
and I shook him

600
00:37:53,770 --> 00:37:55,090
and he was dead.

601
00:37:57,400 --> 00:37:58,790
Just dead.

602
00:38:02,770 --> 00:38:04,460
A man ran over.

603
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:09,650
He had a fish tattoo on his face.

604
00:38:11,380 --> 00:38:13,840
In Volantis the slaves have tattoos

605
00:38:13,840 --> 00:38:16,610
so you know what they are without having to talk to them.

606
00:38:17,260 --> 00:38:19,500
And this man worked on a fishing boat.

607
00:38:20,180 --> 00:38:21,900
And he pushed me out of the way.

608
00:38:23,490 --> 00:38:24,900
You have to understand,

609
00:38:25,280 --> 00:38:28,070
for a slave to push a highborn girl--

610
00:38:28,340 --> 00:38:31,460
that's death for the man, a terrible death.

611
00:38:32,900 --> 00:38:34,790
But he pushed me out of the way

612
00:38:36,410 --> 00:38:40,320
and he started pressing on my brother's chest

613
00:38:40,680 --> 00:38:44,680
again and again and again

614
00:38:44,870 --> 00:38:48,010
until my brother spat out

615
00:38:48,310 --> 00:38:49,860
half of the Rhoyne

616
00:38:51,080 --> 00:38:52,180
and cried out.

617
00:38:52,180 --> 00:38:55,230
And the man cradled his head and told him to be calm.

618
00:39:02,220 --> 00:39:04,300
I decided two things that day.

619
00:39:04,690 --> 00:39:06,460
I would not waste my years

620
00:39:06,460 --> 00:39:10,050
planning dances and masquerades with the other noble ladies.

621
00:39:11,050 --> 00:39:13,760
And when I came of age...

622
00:39:15,210 --> 00:39:17,610
I would never live in a slave city again.

623
00:39:25,420 --> 00:39:26,910
I'm sorry, Your Grace.

624
00:39:26,910 --> 00:39:30,070
You told me of your problems and I've blathered on.

625
00:39:30,070 --> 00:39:32,040
I don't want to marry the Frey girl.

626
00:39:36,690 --> 00:39:38,610
I don't want you to marry her.

627
00:39:41,880 --> 00:39:43,530
But you needed that bridge.

628
00:39:46,830 --> 00:39:48,960
I hope it's a very beautiful bridge.

629
00:40:55,140 --> 00:40:57,420
The sour cherries was all crushed up and ready.

630
00:40:57,420 --> 00:40:58,290
Shut up.

631
00:40:58,470 --> 00:41:00,190
Probably in the piecrust by now.

632
00:41:00,840 --> 00:41:04,030
In the oven, the nice warm oven.

633
00:41:04,030 --> 00:41:06,350
Shut up. What did you bring?

634
00:41:06,730 --> 00:41:08,080
The cheese could be better.

635
00:41:09,110 --> 00:41:10,490
I did get some nice sausages.

636
00:41:10,650 --> 00:41:12,770
What did he want us to do about those guards?

637
00:41:13,360 --> 00:41:14,560
He didn't say.

638
00:41:14,710 --> 00:41:16,430
He just said, "Walk through the gates.

639
00:41:16,430 --> 00:41:17,800
What about the guards?

640
00:41:17,800 --> 00:41:19,670
He didn't say anything about the guards.

641
00:41:19,670 --> 00:41:21,000
What, he left that bit out?

642
00:41:21,470 --> 00:41:23,490
It's a pretty important part, don't you think?

643
00:41:23,830 --> 00:41:26,200
- We have to trust him. - Trust him?

644
00:41:26,570 --> 00:41:28,690
You trusted him to fight with us and you set him free

645
00:41:28,690 --> 00:41:30,780
- and he ran. - I want to go back to the kitchens.

646
00:41:30,780 --> 00:41:33,530
Shut up. Stay here if you're afraid.

647
00:41:36,780 --> 00:41:37,930
Arry, don't.

648
00:42:07,090 --> 00:42:09,310
Away! Reset!

649
00:42:18,100 --> 00:42:21,070
If the wind holds, we'll reach King's Landing in a day.

650
00:42:21,070 --> 00:42:22,140
Will it hold?

651
00:42:22,820 --> 00:42:24,810
Can't make promises for the wind, Your Grace.

652
00:42:26,790 --> 00:42:28,300
Again, pull!

653
00:42:31,980 --> 00:42:33,460
I admire you, Ser Davos.

654
00:42:34,220 --> 00:42:37,250
I thank you, Your Grace. Pleased to hear it.

655
00:42:37,600 --> 00:42:39,820
Some highborn fools call you Onion Knight

656
00:42:39,820 --> 00:42:41,220
and think they insult you.

657
00:42:41,500 --> 00:42:43,510
So you take the onion for your sigil,

658
00:42:43,860 --> 00:42:46,230
sew it on your coat, fly the onion flag.

659
00:42:46,390 --> 00:42:48,170
My son wishes me to change it.

660
00:42:48,170 --> 00:42:50,980
Three mermen with tridents, something like that.

661
00:42:51,710 --> 00:42:54,940
I understand why the older families look down at me.

662
00:42:55,800 --> 00:42:57,810
Do you? Why?

663
00:42:57,810 --> 00:43:00,740
- My father was a crabber. - And?

664
00:43:00,910 --> 00:43:04,620
Well, sons of Lords don't like to break bread with sons of crabbers.

665
00:43:05,050 --> 00:43:06,270
Our hands stink.

666
00:43:06,470 --> 00:43:09,210
And where were those Lords when Storm's End starved?

667
00:43:09,610 --> 00:43:11,230
Many fought bravely for your brother.

668
00:43:11,490 --> 00:43:13,180
Many fought for the Mad King.

669
00:43:14,110 --> 00:43:17,510
You defend these men who insult you behind your back.

670
00:43:18,520 --> 00:43:20,470
Some are happy to do it to my face.

671
00:43:20,470 --> 00:43:21,810
We were forgotten.

672
00:43:22,730 --> 00:43:25,210
Robert and Ned Stark-- they were the heroes,

673
00:43:25,210 --> 00:43:28,800
the glorious rebels marching from battle to battle,

674
00:43:29,330 --> 00:43:31,590
liberating towns from the yoke of the Mad King

675
00:43:31,590 --> 00:43:34,060
while I held Storm's End with 500 men.

676
00:43:34,060 --> 00:43:36,470
- No one has forgotten, Your Grace. - No? Robert did.

677
00:43:36,470 --> 00:43:38,230
He gave Storm's End to Renly after the war.

678
00:43:38,230 --> 00:43:39,950
Renly never fought a day in his life.

679
00:43:39,950 --> 00:43:42,530
- He was only a boy. - Then why'd he give him Storm's End?

680
00:43:46,670 --> 00:43:48,000
First we ate the horses.

681
00:43:48,760 --> 00:43:51,880
We weren't riding anyway, not with the castle surrounded.

682
00:43:52,370 --> 00:43:54,460
We couldn't feed them, so fine, the horses.

683
00:43:54,460 --> 00:43:56,480
Then the cats. Never liked cats.

684
00:43:56,480 --> 00:43:59,250
So fine. I do like dogs.

685
00:43:59,730 --> 00:44:00,990
Good animals. Loyal.

686
00:44:00,990 --> 00:44:03,050
But we ate them. Then the rats.

687
00:44:04,330 --> 00:44:05,550
The night before you slipped through,

688
00:44:05,550 --> 00:44:07,170
I thought my wife was dying.

689
00:44:07,560 --> 00:44:09,540
She couldn't speak anymore, she was so frail.

690
00:44:11,030 --> 00:44:12,920
And then you made it through the lines.

691
00:44:13,420 --> 00:44:16,560
Slipped right through in your little black sailboat with your onions.

692
00:44:16,810 --> 00:44:19,650
And potatoes. Some salted beef, I believe.

693
00:44:19,650 --> 00:44:21,960
Every man in Storm's End wanted to kiss you that night.

694
00:44:21,960 --> 00:44:24,160
I was relieved they did not.

695
00:44:26,580 --> 00:44:29,260
Robert told me to hold Storm's End, so I held it.

696
00:44:31,290 --> 00:44:33,280
Then he told me he was giving it to Renly,

697
00:44:33,470 --> 00:44:34,690
so I gave it up.

698
00:44:34,910 --> 00:44:36,600
Insult or no, I gave it up

699
00:44:37,140 --> 00:44:39,160
because Robert was my older brother and he was the king

700
00:44:39,160 --> 00:44:40,510
and I've always done my duty.

701
00:44:41,590 --> 00:44:44,420
But now I'm the rightful king by every law of Westeros.

702
00:44:45,590 --> 00:44:47,950
And when I sit the Iron Throne, you'll be my Hand.

703
00:44:51,070 --> 00:44:52,140
Your Grace...

704
00:44:54,770 --> 00:44:56,350
I pray I serve you well.

705
00:44:58,140 --> 00:45:00,910
I expect you'll be the first crabber's son to wear the badge.

706
00:45:05,910 --> 00:45:07,240
You're the master of whisperers.

707
00:45:07,240 --> 00:45:09,100
You're supposed to know everything.

708
00:45:09,280 --> 00:45:12,250
No man can be in all rooms at all times.

709
00:45:12,250 --> 00:45:15,130
I have many little birds in the North, My Lord,

710
00:45:15,130 --> 00:45:17,010
but I haven't heard their songs

711
00:45:17,010 --> 00:45:19,730
since Theon Greyjoy captured Winterfell.

712
00:45:19,730 --> 00:45:21,290
The Stark forces are distracted.

713
00:45:21,290 --> 00:45:23,200
Now is the time to strike.

714
00:45:23,760 --> 00:45:24,660
To strike?

715
00:45:25,250 --> 00:45:27,040
My dear nephew, you do see these men

716
00:45:27,040 --> 00:45:28,660
preparing the walls for siege?

717
00:45:29,070 --> 00:45:32,000
You do understand Stannis Baratheon sails this way?

718
00:45:32,650 --> 00:45:35,000
If my Uncle Stannis lands on the shores of King's Landing,

719
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:36,610
I'll ride out to greet him.

720
00:45:36,830 --> 00:45:38,260
A brave choice, Your Grace.

721
00:45:38,660 --> 00:45:41,140
I'm sure your men will line up behind you.

722
00:45:41,780 --> 00:45:43,690
They say Stannis never smiles.

723
00:45:44,910 --> 00:45:47,000
I'll give him a red smile

724
00:45:47,410 --> 00:45:48,650
from ear to ear.

725
00:45:53,980 --> 00:45:56,220
Imagine Stannis's terror.

726
00:45:57,110 --> 00:45:58,280
I am trying.

727
00:46:00,140 --> 00:46:01,420
You're an intelligent man.

728
00:46:01,910 --> 00:46:03,550
I'd like to think I'm an intelligent man.

729
00:46:03,550 --> 00:46:05,150
Oh, no one disputes that, My Lord,

730
00:46:05,150 --> 00:46:07,370
not even the multitudes who despise you.

731
00:46:07,690 --> 00:46:10,340
I wish we could converse as two honest, intelligent men.

732
00:46:10,340 --> 00:46:11,950
I wish we could, too.

733
00:46:14,710 --> 00:46:16,090
What do you want?

734
00:46:16,600 --> 00:46:17,540
Tell me.

735
00:46:18,810 --> 00:46:20,190
If we're going to play,

736
00:46:20,720 --> 00:46:22,460
you'll have to start.

737
00:46:27,050 --> 00:46:30,530
My brother was the youngest Kingsguard in history.

738
00:46:31,740 --> 00:46:34,620
My sister became queen at the age of 19.

739
00:46:36,760 --> 00:46:38,120
When I reached manhood,

740
00:46:38,550 --> 00:46:42,220
my father put me in charge of all the drains and cisterns in Casterly Rock.

741
00:46:42,620 --> 00:46:44,350
A most highborn plumber.

742
00:46:44,750 --> 00:46:46,270
The water never flowed better.

743
00:46:46,670 --> 00:46:48,860
And all the shit found its way to the sea.

744
00:46:49,930 --> 00:46:51,940
I never expected to have any real power.

745
00:46:52,570 --> 00:46:54,600
So when my father named me acting Hand--

746
00:46:54,600 --> 00:46:56,570
You're quite good at being Hand, you know?

747
00:46:56,870 --> 00:46:59,070
Jon Arryn and Ned Stark were good men,

748
00:46:59,730 --> 00:47:00,920
honorable men,

749
00:47:01,790 --> 00:47:04,780
but they disdained the game and those who played.

750
00:47:04,780 --> 00:47:07,360
- You enjoy the game. - I do.

751
00:47:08,130 --> 00:47:09,700
Last thing I expected.

752
00:47:09,870 --> 00:47:11,170
And you play it well.

753
00:47:11,170 --> 00:47:12,590
I'd like to keep playing it.

754
00:47:15,980 --> 00:47:18,560
If Stannis breaches the gates, the game is over.

755
00:47:19,100 --> 00:47:22,930
They say he burns his enemies alive to honor the Lord of Light.

756
00:47:24,040 --> 00:47:25,900
The Lord of Light wants his enemies burned,

757
00:47:25,900 --> 00:47:27,880
the drowned God wants them drowned.

758
00:47:28,640 --> 00:47:30,910
Why are all the Gods such vicious cunts?

759
00:47:31,620 --> 00:47:33,880
Where is the God of tits and wine?

760
00:47:34,820 --> 00:47:36,030
In the Summer Isles,

761
00:47:36,030 --> 00:47:39,460
they worship a fertility goddess with 16 teats.

762
00:47:39,620 --> 00:47:41,320
We should sail there immediately.

763
00:47:43,670 --> 00:47:46,350
This morning I heard a song

764
00:47:47,050 --> 00:47:50,130
all the way from Qarth beyond the Red Waste.

765
00:47:50,690 --> 00:47:52,950
Daenerys Targaryen lives.

766
00:47:54,110 --> 00:47:57,000
A girl at the edge of the world is the least of our problems.

767
00:47:57,170 --> 00:47:58,990
She has three dragons.

768
00:48:00,950 --> 00:48:03,180
But even if what they say is true,

769
00:48:03,180 --> 00:48:05,600
it'll be years before they are fully grown.

770
00:48:06,740 --> 00:48:08,720
And then there will be nowhere to hide.

771
00:48:10,690 --> 00:48:12,620
One game at a time, my friend.

772
00:48:22,800 --> 00:48:24,250
Careful, Khaleesi.

773
00:48:24,930 --> 00:48:28,820
Xaro owns this city and the warlocks have 1,000 eyes watching for you.

774
00:48:30,710 --> 00:48:31,700
I found one--

775
00:48:33,060 --> 00:48:34,710
a ship with a good captain.

776
00:48:35,380 --> 00:48:37,260
She leaves for Astapor tomorrow.

777
00:48:37,260 --> 00:48:39,920
- Astapor? - We cannot stay here.

778
00:48:39,920 --> 00:48:41,150
They have my dragons.

779
00:48:41,150 --> 00:48:43,090
A mother does not flee without her children.

780
00:48:43,260 --> 00:48:44,980
They're not your children.

781
00:48:46,050 --> 00:48:48,020
I know they call you the Mother of Dragons

782
00:48:48,020 --> 00:48:50,700
and I know you love them, but you didn't grow them in your womb.

783
00:48:50,700 --> 00:48:53,470
They didn't suckle at your breast. They are dragons, Khaleesi.

784
00:48:53,630 --> 00:48:55,500
And if we stay in Qarth, we'll die.

785
00:48:55,660 --> 00:48:58,480
You should sail to Astapor. I'm sure you'll be safe there.

786
00:49:01,580 --> 00:49:03,650
You know I would die for you.

787
00:49:04,800 --> 00:49:06,660
I will never abandon you.

788
00:49:07,250 --> 00:49:09,370
I'm sworn to protect you, to serve.

789
00:49:09,370 --> 00:49:11,030
Then serve me.

790
00:49:11,540 --> 00:49:13,970
If my dragons are in the House of the Undying,

791
00:49:13,970 --> 00:49:15,180
then take me there.

792
00:49:15,180 --> 00:49:16,960
That's what the warlock wants.

793
00:49:16,960 --> 00:49:18,720
He told you so himself.

794
00:49:18,720 --> 00:49:21,040
If you enter that place, you will never leave again.

795
00:49:21,660 --> 00:49:24,210
- His magic is strong. - And what of my magic?

796
00:49:24,700 --> 00:49:26,260
You saw me step into the fire.

797
00:49:26,260 --> 00:49:28,920
You watched the witch burn. What did the flames do to me?

798
00:49:28,920 --> 00:49:30,290
Do you remember?

799
00:49:32,960 --> 00:49:36,000
Until my last breath I will remember.

800
00:49:37,860 --> 00:49:40,920
After I have forgotten my mother's face.

801
00:49:45,290 --> 00:49:46,910
They are my children.

802
00:49:48,200 --> 00:49:51,830
And they are the only children I will ever have.

803
00:49:57,930 --> 00:49:59,200
Take me to them.

804
00:50:11,910 --> 00:50:12,940
We should bury them.

805
00:50:14,370 --> 00:50:16,400
I'd leave 'em up a few more days.

806
00:50:16,560 --> 00:50:17,650
Sends a message.

807
00:50:18,860 --> 00:50:20,080
If they haven't got the damn message yet,

808
00:50:20,080 --> 00:50:21,320
a few more days won't help.

809
00:50:22,200 --> 00:50:23,490
As you say.

810
00:50:23,890 --> 00:50:26,260
But it don't hurt to let 'em rot a while longer.

811
00:50:27,780 --> 00:50:28,610
What's this?

812
00:50:28,770 --> 00:50:30,890
Gold for the farmer.

813
00:50:31,360 --> 00:50:33,550
For his trouble.

814
00:50:34,190 --> 00:50:35,340
His troubles are done.

815
00:50:36,410 --> 00:50:37,830
He's feeding the crops now.

816
00:50:38,840 --> 00:50:40,200
His wife, too.

817
00:50:42,420 --> 00:50:44,830
You want to keep a man silent, you silence him.

818
00:51:04,790 --> 00:51:08,210
Got as far as the farm and then doubled back.

819
00:51:10,250 --> 00:51:12,980
Walked through the stream to throw off the hounds.

820
00:51:15,430 --> 00:51:18,490
Hoped this would be the last place they'd think to look.

821
00:51:20,950 --> 00:51:22,180
You're right...

822
00:51:22,690 --> 00:51:23,680
so far.

823
00:51:25,800 --> 00:51:29,340
Who was that out there hung up the gates?

824
00:51:30,880 --> 00:51:32,950
Must have been the farmer's boys.

825
00:51:34,730 --> 00:51:36,720
He killed them and burned them

826
00:51:38,480 --> 00:51:40,760
and passed them off as the little lords?

827
00:51:42,790 --> 00:51:44,000
They mustn't know.

828
00:51:45,700 --> 00:51:47,640
Bran would blame himself.

829
00:51:48,350 --> 00:51:49,910
They'll never hear it from me.

830
00:51:51,750 --> 00:51:53,850
The little lads have suffered enough.

